  "observations": {
    "material": "Actual retained1254 raw and decoded Mid256/High512 read as weathered tangled plant-fibre litter: long flattened grey/olive blades, ochre stems, fraying and dark interstices. Material recognition passes this bounded inspection. Botanical identity and roof/ground use remain interpretations.",
    "distance": "Identical BOX32/16 reductions on native and both decoded tiers retain subdued dark olive/ochre fields and tangled short-stroke/fibre character. Individual new blades are clearer and arrangements are interpreted; exact pixel similarity is not required. Mid loses fine fraying.",
    "repeats": "Full literal X/Y strips and corners show broad fibres ending/restarting against unrelated strands at the exact common wrap line. High1:1 views and magnified source-bound crops make these cuts traceable. The issue is feature continuity, not an aggregate intensity threshold or expected finite-pattern repetition. There is no intentional slab/mortar/contact joint in the native plant-fibre field to justify a straight clipping boundary.",
    "heightXYZNeutralLighting": "Decoded height/XYZ and neutral opposed lights produce recognizable raised fibre networks and lower dark interstices at field scale, without a new perimeter band. Their geometry remains strongly colour-shaped and does not prove individual crossings or pigment-neutral depth. Those limitations are retained; no complete physical-overlap acceptance is claimed while F1 blocks final ART."
  },
